A||||6||sqoach||Hard starting and a few other problems||||9||
Z||000000||sqoach||12-17-2001||10:03 PM||||My 86 SE takes a few cranks before it starts. Sometimes it starts right up, usually when it's been sitting for quite a while.<BR>Also, when my fan kicks on, or if I turn on the a/c the volts drop quite a bit, lights dim, then the volts go back up. And when I use my turn signal, the volts drop a bit and rise with the turn signal flashing.<BR>My battery is good. Probably not even a year old. My belts are tight. Not sure if these problems are releated. Starting seems to be getting worse, but it still always starts. Please help!<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">  <BR><B>86 SE V6 - daily driver</B><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 Sport Coupe 2.5L 5spd (SOLD!)</FONT>||||reg||9
Z||000001||voyagerspe||12-17-2001||11:07 PM||||It could be a bad altenator It could also be that your computer is losing power and (from a corroded/broken/bad wire or bad altenator) If your computer loses power when your car is off it can be hard to start and it can make your car do some strange things. Also check the condition of your battery cables.  oh, and about your battery just because its new dosent mean that its good.<BR>good luck ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-18-2001||12:17 AM||||Sounds alot like a bad alternator or one that is not charging enough.  Check it with a volt meter to be sure.  It's certainly something in the electrical system.  Good luck.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSCF0003a.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||honegod||12-18-2001||08:02 AM||||my 2.8 has a similar starting wierdness, instant when really cold ( has sat for a couple days ), cranks a bit when warm. I suspect a leaky injector. do you get a fuel rich smell on long cranking warm starts ?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||12-18-2001||02:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by honegod:<BR><B>my 2.8 has a similar starting wierdness, instant when really cold ( has sat for a couple days ), cranks a bit when warm. I suspect a leaky injector. do you get a fuel rich smell on long cranking warm starts ?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mine is the same way. If it's been sitting for a few days, all I have to do is twist the key, and it starts right up. If it's recently been run, and I don't press the gas, it doesn't start. Anywhere between half throttle and flat on the floor and it starts up after a few seconds.<BR>I'm thinking leaky injector, too.<BR>Once started, it runs and idles fine. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||BlackARROW||12-18-2001||05:57 PM||||Maybe your battery is new, but what about the cables?  I cleaned mine, removed the rust and corrosion (you know it's a place where water just drops in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>After it dims, your alternator takes the relay and then force to give more volt (so in fact, you're not getting from the battery).  If volts come back, then your alternator looks fine.<P>What I have experienced is battery could not deliver to its full power, and sparks would corrode my neg.pole more and more..until no more start (I would play with the neg.pole and it'll be fine for another start..) In the end, I did my solenoid cables too - and now it starts like a new one (and it's getting pretty cold here up north  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Check that..<P>see ya<P>Black--&gt;<BR>...A Nordic Dude who has to deal with the cold :P<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||sqoach||12-19-2001||12:22 AM||||I'm not sure how old the alternator is. I plan on getting a higher-amperage one anyway. I'll check the cables too. I don't want to replace them, because I plan on moving the battery sometime in the near future. Today it seemed to start better after it was warmed up. This is weird.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">||||reg||1
